    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Designing for the \"Oops\"\r\n\r\nChoose one of the following user complaints about the Concert App (from Level 1). Design the UI for what should appear on screen instead. \r\n\r\n> The Infinite Spinner: \"I clicked 'Buy', but the loading icon just spun forever.\"\r\n\r\n> The Ghost Map: “The page loaded, but the seat map is blank.”\r\n\r\n> The Code Crash: \"I clicked my profile and the whole app just crashed.\"\r\n\r\n::: details [**What should appear on screen?**]\r\n- **The Message:** Explain what happened in plain English. Avoid using \"Error 404\" or \"Null\".\r\n- **The Action:** Give the user a clear next step, e.g., a \"Retry\" button, a \"Contact Support\" link, or a \"Return to Home\" option.\r\n- **The Tone Check:** Ensure the tone is calm and helpful. Avoid scary icons or blaming the user.\r\n:::",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
    "submittable": "false",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "false",
